---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service | aiPressHQ"
  description="The terms that govern using aiPressHQ's articles, trackers, and saved-stories feature."
>
  <section class="legal-page" aria-labelledby="legal-title">
    <header class="legal-header">
      <span class="label">aiPressHQ / Terms of Service</span>
      <h1 id="legal-title">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated August 6, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose legal-body">
      <p>
        These terms govern your use of aiPressHQ. By reading and using this site, you agree to
        them. If you don't agree, the only recourse is to stop using the site — there's no
        account to cancel.
      </p>

      <h2>What aiPressHQ is</h2>
      <p>
        aiPressHQ publishes news briefs, explainers, comparisons, trackers, analysis, and
        tutorials about artificial intelligence. Our editorial approach — how we source, label,
        and correct coverage — is described on the <a href="/about/">Our method</a> page, which
        is part of these terms by reference.
      </p>

      <h2>Not professional advice</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing on aiPressHQ is financial, legal, medical, or other professional advice.
        Product capabilities, pricing, availability, and policies described in our coverage can
        change or vary by account, region, or plan, and can be out of date by the time you read
        them. Verify anything you intend to rely on against the primary source linked in the
        article before acting on it.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy and corrections</h2>
      <p>
        We try to get things right and link the sources our reporting is built on. When a
        factual error is found, we correct the relevant passage rather than silently rewriting
        the record. That said, the content is provided "as is," without warranty of accuracy,
        completeness, or fitness for a particular purpose.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        Articles, graphics, and the aiPressHQ name and marks are owned by aiPressHQ unless
        otherwise credited. You're welcome to quote short excerpts with attribution and a link
        back to the original article. Reproducing or republishing full articles, or using our
        content to train or fine-tune a model, requires our prior written permission.
      </p>

      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        Our articles link to the official documents, product pages, and other outlets that
        anchor a story's central claims. We don't control those sites and aren't responsible
        for their content, accuracy, or availability.
      </p>

      <h2>Saved stories</h2>
      <p>
        The "save for later" feature stores your bookmarked articles in your browser's local
        storage on your own device — there's no account and nothing is backed up on our end.
        Clearing your browser data, or switching browsers or devices, will clear your saved
        list. See the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for how this works.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability of the service</h2>
      <p>
        We may change, add, remove, or discontinue any part of the site — including specific
        articles, trackers, or features — at any time and without notice.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, aiPressHQ is not liable for any damages arising
        from your use of, or inability to use, the site or its content, including decisions made
        in reliance on information published here.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        These terms may be updated as the site changes. Continuing to use aiPressHQ after an
        update means you accept the revised terms. The date above reflects the latest change.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms can be sent to <a
          href="mailto:hello@aipresshq.com">hello@aipresshq.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
